  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard in Kibana, and I haven't confirmed the rule runs without errors.\n\n**Fields:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` has `timestamp`, `bytes`, `clientip`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `referer`, `url`, `extension` and `tags`. `response` (the HTTP status code) is text, so the aggregations use `response.keyword`.\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-e4b1f9c9 Web logs overview` (id `fab576d8-0e36-4334-a5be-e958e8e73dcb`) has five panels:\n- Three metric panels: total requests, average bytes and total bytes.\n- A line chart of requests over time.\n- A bar chart of requests by response code.\n\n**Rule:** `EFF-e4b1f9c9 5xx spike` (id `7210d7c6-8c1b-45b6-b9da-cf87089097a4`) is an Elasticsearch query rule.\n- **Check:** it runs every minute over the last 5 minutes.\n- **Trigger:** it fires when more than 10 documents have a `response.keyword` starting with \"5\".\n- **Actions:** none are attached, so it will record alerts in Kibana but not send notifications anywhere. No connectors are configured.",
